  "summary": "An instrument air dryer removes water vapour from compressed air so control valves and instruments never see condensation or ice. This heated blower-purge type has two desiccant towers: one dries the air while the other is regenerated by heated ambient air from a blower, so very little dried compressed air is used for purging.",
